# Golden-master output digests, not credentials.
#
# golden/pre-extraction/digests-*.txt pins one SHA-256 per canonical parameter
# combination, in the form `canon__<combination> <sha256>`. The 64-character hex
# string matches the audit's long-token heuristic and is reported as an API key.
#
# Deliberately narrow: the exemption requires the `canon__` key prefix, so a real
# secret pasted into the same file is still caught. The hex run is matched as
# 20-or-more characters because these lines are 170-187 characters long and the
# audit truncates its snippet at 160, cutting the digest short.
^canon__\S+\s+[0-9a-f]{20,}
